{"surah": 97, "verses": [{"ayah": 1, "text": "إِنَّآ أَنزَلْنَٰهُ فِى لَيْلَةِ ٱلْقَدْرِ ", "translation": "Indeed, We sent it [i.e., the Qur’ān] down during the Night of Decree.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "إِنَّآ", "translit": "ٓāَّnِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "أَنزَلْنَٰهُ", "translit": "ُhَٰnْlَznَaʾ", "root": "نزل"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "فِى", "translit": "àِf", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "لَيْلَةِ", "translit": "ِẗَlْyَl", "root": "ليل"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "ٱلْقَدْرِ", "translit": "ِrْdَqْlٱ", "root": "قدر"}], "hasIhya": true}, {"ayah": 2, "text": "وَمَآ أَدْرَىٰكَ مَا لَيْلَةُ ٱلْقَدْرِ ", "translation": "And what can make you know what is the Night of Decree?", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَمَآ", "translit": "ٓāَmَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "أَدْرَىٰكَ", "translit": "َkٰàَrْdَaʾ", "root": "دري"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "مَا", "translit": "āَm", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "لَيْلَةُ", "translit": "ُẗَlْyَl", "root": "ليل"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "ٱلْقَدْرِ", "translit": "ِrْdَqْlٱ", "root": "قدر"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 3, "text": "لَيْلَةُ ٱلْقَدْرِ خَيْرٌ مِّنْ أَلْفِ شَهْرٍ ", "translation": "The Night of Decree is better than a thousand months.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "لَيْلَةُ", "translit": "ُẗَlْyَl", "root": "ليل"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "ٱلْقَدْرِ", "translit": "ِrْdَqْlٱ", "root": "قدر"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "خَيْرٌ", "translit": "ٌrْyَhk", "root": "خير"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "مِّنْ", "translit": "ْnِّm", "root": ""}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "أَلْفِ", "translit": "ِfْlَaʾ", "root": "الف"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "شَهْرٍ", "translit": "ٍrْhَhs", "root": "شهر"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 4, "text": "تَنَزَّلُ ٱلْمَلَٰٓئِكَةُ وَٱلرُّوحُ فِيهَا بِإِذْنِ رَبِّهِم مِّن كُلِّ أَمْرٍ ", "translation": "The angels and the Spirit [i.e., Gabriel] descend therein by permission of their Lord for every matter.[1]", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "تَنَزَّلُ", "translit": "ُlَّzَnَt", "root": "نزل"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "ٱلْمَلَٰٓئِكَةُ", "translit": "ُẗَkِyʾَٰٓlَmْlٱ", "root": "ملك"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "وَٱلرُّوحُ", "translit": "ُḥwُّrlٱَw", "root": "روح"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "فِيهَا", "translit": "āَhyِf", "root": ""}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "بِإِذْنِ", "translit": "ِnْhdِiʾِb", "root": "اذن"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "رَبِّهِم", "translit": "mِhِّbَr", "root": "ربب"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "مِّن", "translit": "nِّm", "root": ""}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "كُلِّ", "translit": "ِّlُk", "root": "كلل"}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "أَمْرٍ", "translit": "ٍrْmَaʾ", "root": "امر"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 5, "text": "سَلَٰمٌ هِىَ حَتَّىٰ مَطْلَعِ ٱلْفَجْرِ ", "translation": "Peace it is[1] until the emergence of dawn.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "سَلَٰمٌ", "translit": "ٌmَٰlَs", "root": "سلم"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "هِىَ", "translit": "َàِh", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "حَتَّىٰ", "translit": "ٰàَّtَḥ", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "مَطْلَعِ", "translit": "ِʿعَlْṭَm", "root": "طلع"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "ٱلْفَجْرِ", "translit": "ِrْjgَfْlٱ", "root": "فجر"}], "hasIhya": false}], "tafsir": {"1": [{"arabic": "ومنها التدريج في البيان كقوله عز وجل ﴿ شهر رمضان الذي أنزل فيه القرآن ﴾ {} إذ لم يظهر به أنه ليل أو نهار وبان بقوله عز وجل ﴿ إنا أنزلناه في ليلة مباركة ﴾ {} ولم يظهر به أي ليلة فظهر بقوله تعالى ﴿ إنا أنزلناه في ليلة القدر ﴾ {} وربما يظن في الظاهر الاختلاف بين هذه الآيات فهذا وأمثاله مما لا يغني فيه إلا النقل والسماع", "english": "And among them is the gradual clarification in the explanation, as in His saying, the Mighty and Majestic: 'The month of Ramadan in which the Quran was revealed' (2:185), since it did not become clear by it whether it was night or day, and it became clear by His saying, the Mighty and Majestic: 'Indeed, We sent it down during a blessed night' (44:3), and it did not become clear by it which night, so it became clear by His saying, the Exalted: 'Indeed, We sent it down during the Night of Decree (Laylat al-Qadr)' (97:1). And perhaps it is thought in the apparent meaning that there is a difference between these verses, so this and its like are matters in which nothing avails except transmission (al-Naql) and hearing (al-Samāʿ).", "book_file": "vol1_Vol1-book-8.doc.txt", "book_title": "Etiquette of Quran Recitation", "content_type": "dhikr", "topic": "Al-Ghazali on the virtue and practice of remembering God, from 'Etiquette of Quran Recitation'", "badge": "Dhikr"}, {"arabic": "فعسى الشيطان أن لا يحوم على قلبه فينظر إلى ملكوت السماء وليلة القدر عبارة عن الليلة التي ينكشف فيها شيء من الملكوت وهو المراد بقوله تعالى: ﴿ إنا أنزلناه في ليلة القدر ﴾{} ومن جعل بين قلبه وبين صدره مخلاة من الطعام فهو عنه محجوب ومن أخلى معدته فلا يكفيه ذلك لرفع الحجاب ما لم يخل همته عن غير الله عز وجل وذلك هو الأمر كله ومبدأ جميع ذلك تقليل الطعام", "english": "Perhaps Satan will not hover over his heart so he may gaze upon the Kingdom of the Heavens (Malakut al-Sama'), and the Night of Power (Laylat al-Qadr) is an expression for the night in which something of the Kingdom (Malakut) is unveiled, and this is what is intended by His saying, the Exalted: \"Indeed, We sent it down during the Night of Power (Laylat al-Qadr).\" And whoever places between his heart (Qalb) and his chest a feedbag of food is veiled from it, and whoever empties his stomach, that does not suffice him to lift the veil unless he empties his aspiration (Himmah) from other than God, the Mighty and Majestic, and that is the entire matter, and the beginning of all of that is reducing food.", "book_file": "vol1_Vol1-book-6.doc.txt", "book_title": "Mysteries of Fasting", "content_type": "dhikr", "topic": "Al-Ghazali on the virtue and practice of remembering God, from 'Mysteries of Fasting'", "badge": "Dhikr"}, {"arabic": "يقرأ في كل ركعة بفاتحة الكتاب مرة وإنا أنزلناه في ليلة القدر ثلاث مرات وقل هو الله أحد اثنتي عشرة مرة", "english": "He recites in each unit of prayer (rak'ah) the Opening (Al-Fatihah) of the Book once and 'Indeed, We sent it down during the Night of Decree (Laylat al-Qadr)' three times and 'Say: He is Allah, the One' twelve times.", "book_file": "vol1_Vol1-book-4.doc.txt", "book_title": "Mysteries of Prayer", "content_type": "dua", "topic": "Al-Ghazali on supplications and their spiritual significance, from 'Mysteries of Prayer'", "badge": "Du'a"}, {"arabic": "وقوله تعالى ﴿ إنا أنزلناه في ليلة القدر ﴾ {} أراد القرآن وما سبق له ذكر", "english": "And His saying, the Exalted: 'Indeed, We sent it down during the Night of Decree (Laylat al-Qadr)' {} He intended the Quran and what preceded it of mention.", "book_file": "vol1_Vol1-book-8.doc.txt", "book_title": "Etiquette of Quran Recitation", "content_type": "dhikr", "topic": "Al-Ghazali on the virtue and practice of remembering God, from 'Etiquette of Quran Recitation'", "badge": "Dhikr"}]}, "wordTiming": {"abdulbasit": {"1": [[1, 400, 2663], [2, 2663, 4605], [3, 4605, 5329], [4, 5329, 6575], [5, 6575, 7952]], "2": [[1, 350, 1675], [2, 1675, 3038], [3, 3038, 3555], [4, 3555, 4411], [5, 4411, 5357]], "3": [[1, 350, 1266], [2, 1266, 2278], [3, 2278, 3045], [4, 3045, 3780], [5, 3780, 4462], [6, 4462, 5122]], "4": [[1, 400, 1534], [2, 1534, 3443], [3, 3443, 5149], [4, 5149, 6342], [5, 6342, 7368], [6, 7368, 8478], [7, 8478, 9301], [8, 9301, 9957], [9, 9957, 10721]], "5": [[1, 350, 1048], [2, 1048, 1501], [3, 1501, 2491], [4, 2491, 3401], [5, 3401, 4260]]}, "husary": {"1": [[1, 400, 3712], [2, 3712, 6553], [3, 6553, 7613], [4, 7613, 9436], [5, 9436, 11450]], "2": [[1, 400, 2626], [2, 2626, 4916], [3, 4916, 5785], [4, 5785, 7222], [5, 7222, 8811]], "3": [[1, 400, 2125], [2, 2125, 4031], [3, 4031, 5475], [4, 5475, 6859], [5, 6859, 8143], [6, 8143, 9386]], "4": [[1, 400, 2199], [2, 2199, 5229], [3, 5229, 7937], [4, 7937, 9831], [5, 9831, 11459], [6, 11459, 13220], [7, 13220, 14527], [8, 14527, 15568], [9, 15568, 16779]], "5": [[1, 350, 1588], [2, 1588, 2391], [3, 2391, 4148], [4, 4148, 5763], [5, 5763, 7287]]}, "minshawi": {"1": [[1, 200, 3602], [2, 3602, 5643], [3, 5643, 6412], [4, 6412, 771